# Story 87: Pipeline Events (##>) (45s)
# Hook: Lines starting with double-hash-greater-than bypass the shell and fly straight to NATS.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-087-pipeline-events.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Lines starting with double-hash-greater-than bypass the shell and fly straight to NATS.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh and split a second pane. We'll have this worker listen to the first pane's shared output.

[00:09.0 --> 00:18.0]
In rysh mode, ##pane listen forwards another pane's shared output here. Event payloads arrive without an alias prefix.

[00:18.0 --> 00:25.0]
Hop to the orchestrator pane and switch it to rysh mode so we can emit a pipeline event.

[00:25.0 --> 00:34.0]
##>event:print: takes a payload. This line never touches the PTY -- it publishes straight to the pane's NATS output topic.

[00:34.0 --> 00:42.0]
Send as many as you like. Each event is a clean line in the shared output buffer, visible to every listening pane.

[00:42.0 --> 00:45.0]
##> is your event bus -- shell-free messages between panes.

